┌ Guide ─ flk help cheatsheet ─ 78% ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ # flk cheat sheet                                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ What's going on?                                                                                                                                             │
│   flk context                        this app: machines, ports, what to do next                                                                              │
│   flk context --all                  every app on this host                                                                                                  │
│   flk doctor                         host health, each problem with its fix                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Run an app (in its directory, with a Dockerfile, flk.toml or fly.toml)                                                                                       │
│   flk launch --no-deploy             write flk.toml if missing, register the app                                                                             │
│   flk volumes create data --size 1   one per machine, for [[mounts]] source = "data"                                                                         │
│   flk secrets set KEY=VALUE --stage  env vars kept out of flk.toml                                                                                           │
│   flk deploy                         build, then create or update the machines                                                                               │
│   flk status                         machines, IPs, states                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Look inside                                                                                                                                                  │
│   flk logs [-i ID] [-n 200] [-f]     app output and boot messages                                                                                            │
│   flk console [ID]                   type to the app (server consoles); leave: Ctrl-b d                                                                      │
│   flk console --send "say hi"        one line to the app, no attaching (--wait-log REGEX: see the answer)                                                    │
│   flk machine status ID              everything flk knows about a machine                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Start and stop                                                                                                                                               │
│   flk machine stop|start|restart ID  stop stays stopped, also across reboots                                                                                 │
│   flk resume                         start everything that should be running                                                                                 │
│   flk stop-all                       stop everything gracefully; resume brings it back                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Reach it                                                                                                                                                     │
│   http://MACHINE_IP:PORT             machine IPs (flk status) work from the host                                                                             │
│   [flk] http_port = N                serve [http_service] on host port N (the LAN too)                                                                       │
│   [[services.ports]] port = N        same for [[services]]; then: flk ports                                                                                  │
│   not 127.0.0.1                      use the host's LAN IP, or: flk proxy N [ID]                                                                             │
│   [flk] bind = "10.47.11.3"          forward only on that host address (host.toml: bind, address)                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Change things                                                                                                                                                │
│   edit flk.toml, then flk deploy     flk config show: what flk understood                                                                                    │
│   flk scale count N                  new machines need their own volumes                                                                                     │
│   flk secrets set|unset ...          restarts machines (unless --stage)                                                                                      │
│   flk releases rollback [vN]         back to an older release (image + config)                                                                               │
│   [checks.NAME] type = "log"|"tcp"|"http"   deploys wait for these; failures roll back                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Data                                                                                                                                                         │
│   flk volumes backup [NAME]          copy to backup_dir (~/.config/flk/host.toml) or --to DIR                                                                │
│   flk volumes backups                list them; restore NAME [BACKUP] with the machine stopped                                                               │
│   flk volumes verify [NAME]          check the latest backup (e2fsck -n + verify hook), no stop                                                              │
│   flk volumes restore NAME --as NEW  a backup into a new volume (test a restore, no stop)                                                                    │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ↑↓ pgup/dn scroll  / search  n/N match  esc topics                                                                                                           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
